    "result": "Perfect! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n**1. Missing named export in `src/finetune/index.js`**\n   - The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export\n   - Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n   - Kept them in the default export for backward compatibility\n\n**2. Toxicity metric receiving wrong parameters in `src/eval/metrics.js`**\n   - The `toxicityMetric` function was receiving `references` as the second parameter from `runEvaluations`, but treated it as `bannedTerms`\n   - This caused references like `'hello'` and `'friendly world'` to be interpreted as banned terms, incorrectly flagging benign outputs as toxic\n   - Updated the function to accept `references` but ignore it, always using the default banned terms\n   - The function now correctly computes toxicity scores based only on the default banned term list\n\n## Test Results\n\u2705 All 28 tests passing across 8 test files\n- `src/finetune/governance.test.js`: 5/5 \u2713\n- `src/eval/index.test.js`: 3/3 \u2713\n- All other tests remain passing",
